<title>USA: First Savings Bank of NJ CEO to retire.</title>
<headline>First Savings Bank of NJ CEO to retire.</headline>
<dateline>BAYONNE, N.J. 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Savings Bank of New Jersey SLA and Bayonne Bankshares MHC, its holding company, said on Monday Patrick Nilan planned to retire as chief executive officer and president effective June 30.</p>
<p>The company said its chief operating officer, Michael Nilan, would succeed Patrick Nilan, his father.</p>
<p>Patrick Nilan would remain a director and chairman of the board, the company said.</p>
